  Two things in it are worth your attention specifically. The [1massumption[0m in the cutover section — that your future
  backend will accept a client-supplied device id and return a stable user id — is unverified, and it's written as an
  assumption rather than a fact for that reason; it's the one thing that could make part of this design wrong. And the
  [1msecurity section[0m states that the login log is not an audit trail and can be freely edited by the user. If anyone
  downstream is expecting this to answer "who logged in" in a way that holds up under scrutiny, that expectation needs
  correcting now rather than after the backend lands.

